355 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Our July Newsletter is finally ready! This special issue features captivating stories and essays from emerging writers, curated with care by the VSA Team. It includes a mix of fiction and non-fiction that explores the depths of human connection and understanding.)
/Pg 7 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
356 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Esteemed researcher Prof. Simon Baron-Cohen noted in his book Zero Degrees of Empathy, "...empathy itself is the most valuable resource in our world. Given this assertion, it is puzzling that in the school or parenting curriculum empathy figures hardly at all..." In line with this, volumes of neuroscience research now show that nurturing the empathic circuits in our brains makes us more peaceful, healthier, and resilient. Recognising others' feelings enhances our relationships with family, friends, and colleagues.)
/Pg 7 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
357 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Each piece in this issue showcases students' deep understanding of empathy's importance in our world. These stories embody the spirit of empathy in action, reflecting our commitment to fostering a more compassionate and connected society. Enjoy these inspiring journeys and let them encourage you to embrace empathy in your own life.)
/Pg 7 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
358 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText <>
/Pg 7 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
359 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Each year, when we open submissions for the Elaine Hobson Memorial Literary Festival, we confront the challenge of ranking entries. Despite blind marking, it's ironic to judge these essays and creative pieces, as art is inherently subjective, and every judge has their unique perspective. We congratulate the selected top four but firmly believe every entry is a winner.)
/Pg 7 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
360 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (To all writers, if your name isn't on the winners' list, don't be disheartened. Be proud of your work. We thoroughly enjoyed reading your stories and essays. Most importantly, continue writing meaningful pieces that will inspire our global community. Our next Global Empathy Conference will commence in May 2025 at the University of California, Silicon Valley. If you would like to participate, share your next piece on empathy. Together, let's continue to explore the depths of human connection and inspire a global wave of understanding and compassion.)
/Pg 7 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
