571 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (As I sat in the classroom on the second day of the new year, memories flooded back to me like an unexpected gust of wind, reminding me of my struggles with language barriers when I first moved here. A cool breeze swept over my face as I looked up to see Denise enter through the door. You could tell she was different from the lot. She had curly locks that hung from her face, and big eyes full of wonder. However, there was an undeniable barrier - she didn't speak English.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
572 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Professor Kashyap's entrance brought a shift in the atmosphere, his authoritative demeanour casting a shadow over the room. His gaze lingered on Denise, a sardonic smile playing at the corners of his lips. "Settle down, class," he declared, his tone dripping with sarcasm. "We have a newcomer today, though it seems she missed the memo that this is an English class." )
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
573 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Denise, undeterred by the professor's barbed remarks, retrieved her notebook, her determination unwavering. Yet, as Professor Kashyap directed his mocking words towards her, a sense of unease settled over the room like a thick fog. "How exactly do you plan to understand what I say, missy?" he taunted, his voice laced with condescension. Denise met his gaze with a mixture of confusion and defiance, her inability to comprehend his words apparent to all. )
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
574 0 obj
<<
