/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (When the weeks had long since dragged themselves into months and the weather turned to a vengeful force beating burning sunlight down onto passersby, I found myself cowering under the slender shade of a windowsill. As the sidewalk seared my skin through, I glanced upwards in search of clouds. Instead, I was greeted by a face, encircled by brilliant sunlight, peering out from an upstairs window. Your face. Just as soon as I saw it, though, you were gone. Vanished, back into your air-conditioned palace. I should have known. )
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [3]
>>
