626 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Empathy is what stops the world from dividing into a hierarchy where people are separated based on their beliefs and ideals. It prevents the world from falling into a vengeful chaos where we dehumanise one another, reducing ourselves to versions of superficial worth, a world without compassion for other beings where we push species to the brink of extinction for our selfish gain. Already, the modern world is moving scarily towards apathy, a place where we burn forests to the ground for exploitive gain of oil or land resources, where we desensitise ourselves to the realities of the world around us with a quick swipe of our finger, promoting an idea of blissful ignorance to replace one of truth. )
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
627 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (The lens through which humans see the world, empathy is how we connect with the people around us. We are slowly but surely forgetting our intrinsic need for empathy and the vital role that it plays in humanity, moving towards a reality of isolation and competition, looking away and walking past without hesitation as someone next to us trips and falls to their knees, feeling fictitiously autonomous until we, too, fall. We forget how we observe and understand the flaws and                                                               )
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
