/ActualText (When I started running in middle school, I was not fast at all. I never made the Junior Olympics team, I struggled to break through in high school and was always one step behind those who started earlier, but I had a dream. I can still recall the first time I watched the Olympics as a wide-eyed child, filled with wonder at the sheer magnificence of the athletes. And now I have my chance. Today, Tokyo presents an opportunity like no other, for me, Isaiah Jewett, to make the Olympic finals. )
