936 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (Empathy is a skill. It is the ability to understand the thoughts and feelings of those around us, which we use to put ourselves into their shoes. In some ways, it connects us with the world and the emotions that make it turn. )
/E (Empathy is a skill. It is the ability to understand the thoughts and feelings of those around us, which we use to put ourselves into their shoes. In some ways, it connects us with the world and the emotions that make it turn. )
/Pg 49 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
937 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (Empathy has three types: compassionate, cognitive, and emotional. Simply put, compassionate empathy is empathy in action. When we extend our aid to people in need, compassionate empathy comes into play. Cognitive empathy is the ability to detect another's feelings. It is the first layer of empathy on which the other two rest. Lastly, emotional empathy is "when you feel physically along with the other person, as though their emotions were contagious." \(Goleman, D. \(2011\). Different kinds of empathy. Key Step Media.\) )
/E (Empathy has three types: compassionate, cognitive, and emotional. Simply put, compassionate empathy is empathy in action. When we extend our aid to people in need, compassionate empathy comes into play. Cognitive empathy is the ability to detect another's feelings. It is the first layer of empathy on which the other two rest. Lastly, emotional empathy is "when you feel physically along with the other person, as though their emotions were contagious." \(Goleman, D. \(2011\). Different kinds of empathy. Key Step Media.\) )
/Pg 49 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
938 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (Experiences and empathy combine throughout our lifetime to build our ideals, ethics, and character. If a person is suffering, cognitive empathy allows us to detect this suffering, and compassionate empathy spurs us to extend a helping hand. However, the involvement of emotional empathy is more complex. If a child witnesses a person performing an activity, the child tends to associate that person's emotions with the activity. As children instinctually gravitate towards joy, they tend to perform activities they associate with it. )
/E (Experiences and empathy combine throughout our lifetime to build our ideals, ethics, and character. If a person is suffering, cognitive empathy allows us to detect this suffering, and compassionate empathy spurs us to extend a helping hand. However, the involvement of emotional empathy is more complex. If a child witnesses a person performing an activity, the child tends to associate that person's emotions with the activity. As children instinctually gravitate towards joy, they tend to perform activities they associate with it. )
/Pg 49 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
939 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (These ideas portray empathy as a guru within, which guides the actions and ideals of the individual. As a mentor of the character, it holds tremendous influence over our words, deeds, and thoughts. The Japanese explore these ideas through Omoiyari, the concept of empathy and consideration. This idea is embedded within Japanese society and is inculcated in children early on. By exposing them to a compassionate society, Japan has enabled the growth of empathy within their youth, allowing them to develop respect, insight, and a drive to better their community. I experienced firsthand the empathy of the Japanese people when I visited the country. The citizens went so far as to draw maps for us and walk us to train stations to ensure we would find our way. )
/E (These ideas portray empathy as a guru within, which guides the actions and ideals of the individual. As a mentor of the character, it holds tremendous influence over our words, deeds, and thoughts. The Japanese explore these ideas through Omoiyari, the concept of empathy and consideration. This idea is embedded within Japanese society and is inculcated in children early on. By exposing them to a compassionate society, Japan has enabled the growth of empathy within their youth, allowing them to develop respect, insight, and a drive to better their community. I experienced firsthand the empathy of the Japanese people when I visited the country. The citizens went so far as to draw maps for us and walk us to train stations to ensure we would find our way. )
/Pg 49 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
940 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (However, the severe want of empathy in the present is as plain as day. Acts of kindness, words of understanding, or thoughts of consideration are lacking in the vast majority. As a teenager going into high school, I had not expected the weight of my actions to be so crushing. Every step I took was scrutinized by the many eyes trained on me. Each one judged, calculated, and whispered, till I convinced myself that their standards were more suffocating than I could take. My first panic attack was in high school, and every relapse came with a fresh bout of judgement. Part of the blame goes to the society that did not have the empathy to withhold their judgement. Even with the thousands of teenagers having the same problem, society cannot deign to grant us the bare minimum, the empathy of silence, that could have prevented our conditions. )
/E (However, the severe want of empathy in the present is as plain as day. Acts of kindness, words of understanding, or thoughts of consideration are lacking in the vast majority. As a teenager going into high school, I had not expected the weight of my actions to be so crushing. Every step I took was scrutinized by the many eyes trained on me. Each one judged, calculated, and whispered, till I convinced myself that their standards were more suffocating than I could take. My first panic attack was in high school, and every relapse came with a fresh bout of judgement. Part of the blame goes to the society that did not have the empathy to withhold their judgement. Even with the thousands of teenagers having the same problem, society cannot deign to grant us the bare minimum, the empathy of silence, that could have prevented our conditions. )
/Pg 49 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
