/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (Other studies in humans have shown that mere perception of another individual's pain activates the pain-related neural network in the observer, as though the observer was experiencing pain. These neural networks have Mirror Neurons, specialised cells in the brain that fire signals when we see another person acting. Brain imaging techniques have found increased activity in the Mirror Neurons when we empathise with other people's pain or joy. )
/E (Other studies in humans have shown that mere perception of another individual's pain activates the pain-related neural network in the observer, as though the observer was experiencing pain. These neural networks have Mirror Neurons, specialised cells in the brain that fire signals when we see another person acting. Brain imaging techniques have found increased activity in the Mirror Neurons when we empathise with other people's pain or joy. )
/Pg 55 0 R
/K [7]
