/T (She began emptying the contents, and then she tossed the lunch box into the weed and muck. She dusted her hands, proud of her work, and the little group walked off, sniggering.  Leaving me in their dust.  I just wanted to be friends with them.  Half an hour later, I was still crouched there. My tears bounced off the little pebbles and into puddles. I was a baby.  I heard footsteps getting louder behind me.  I whipped my head around, prepared for the worst. )
