/T ( I think the highlight was definitely interviewing the son of a friend of my mother's, who has epilepsy. He was diagnosed at age eight and is currently twelve. It was so enlightening to learn more about it and one of the main reasons I wrote my story about him was because of how little we know or talk about epilepsy. About 50 million people have epilepsy, making it an extremely common affliction that isn't discussed nearly enough. I was so curious to learn about his experiences and how different his world is from mine.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                      - Tanisha Desai)
